          "=",
          ",",
          "The general single vector meson exchange graph attached to baryons",
          "(straight lines) and pions (dashed lines) or external sources (wiggly lines) like e.g.",
          "the photon. The shaded areas denote the loop expansion of the respective vertices.",
          "Notice that the circle-cross is completely embedded in the shaded area on the right.",
          "one correspondence between the loop expansion and the expansion in small",
          "momenta and meson masses. There is no a priori reason why multi–loop graphs",
          "can not even modify the lowest order results, see also ref.[1]. We will now",
          "show that in the tensor and in the vector formulation, these type of graphs",
          "only contribute to subleading orders, i.e. they do neither modify the Weinberg",
          "term nor the leading contributions to the anomalous magnetic moments of the",
          "octet baryons. This is intimately related to the form of the V φφ and VµAµ",
          "Consider ﬁrst the vector formulation. The two–pion–vector vertex is propor-",
          "(p′ −p)ν (k + p′ −p)ν kµ",
          "where the vector carries momentum p′−p and the in–coming (out–going) pion",
          "k (k + p′ −p), see Fig.3. This obviously vanishes in forward direction, p′ →p.",
          "Similarly, the photon–vector meson vertex is proportional to (p′ −p)ν(p′ −p)µ,",
          "which is at least of order q2 and thus can not contribute to the leading order",
